# {{.ProjectName}}

A Quantum suite application generated with `nucleus new --template suite`:
a **Nucleus** application whose domain runs on the **Quark** ORM, with the
**Orbit** admin panel mounted on top and both bridges between them wired.

- **Live SQL feed** — the shop module's HTTP handlers query Quark through a
  client wrapped with `orbit/quarkbridge`: every statement appears in
  Orbit's live view, correlated to the request, with bind arguments
  redacted by default.
- **Data Studio on Quark** — Orbit's Data Studio is backed by
  `orbit/quarkdatasource` over the same models (`orbit.Config.DataSource`),
  so `/admin` browses and edits them.

Two Quark models (`Author`, `Article` with a `belongs_to`) on one {{.Database}}
database shared by the application (admin accounts) and the domain schema.

## Run it

```bash
go run .
```

`nucleus new` already resolved the suite modules and the {{.Database}} drivers
(`go get` + `go mod tidy`); if the project was scaffolded with `--offline`,
run those two commands first (the scaffold printed them). The app listens on
the port in `nucleus.yml` (`{{.Port}}`).

## Try it

```bash
curl -s localhost:{{.Port}}/api/articles
curl -s -X POST localhost:{{.Port}}/api/articles \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d '{"author_id":1,"title":"probe","body":"live feed"}'
```

Then open **http://localhost:{{.Port}}/admin** — user `admin`, password
`quickstart` unless `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD` was set before the first
boot (a development credential; set the variable before the app faces
anyone but you):

- **Live view**: hit the API and watch the Quark statements arrive with
  their `request_id`.
- **Data Studio**: browse `Author`/`Article`, create or edit a record, and
  see it through the public API.

`go test ./...` boots the shop module on an in-process application and
drives the same API, duplicate-title probe included.

## What to read

- [`main.go`](main.go) — the whole wiring: Quark client + migrate/seed,
  `quarkdatasource.Register[T]`, `orbit.Config.DataSource`, and the two
  `Mount` calls.
- [`shop/module.go`](shop/module.go) — the module's own policy rows and
  CSRF exemption, the bridge derivation in `OnStart`
  (`client.WithOptions(quark.WithMiddleware(quarkbridge.New(rt.Observability())))`)
  and the handlers.
- `nucleus.yml` and `rbac_policy.csv` — the framework's own configuration
  and the rows for its built-in endpoints; the shop routes and `/admin`
  bring their own.

## Add your next feature

```bash
nucleus generate module notes --mount
```

writes a self-contained slice under `internal/notes/` and mounts it in
`main.go`; `--data quark` renders its storage on the Quark ORM the shop
module already uses.

## Versions

The suite modules were fetched from the module proxy at their latest
published tags. Nucleus tags before Orbit in every release: right after a
Nucleus release, `orbit` may still pin the previous Nucleus minor — `go`
keeps the higher of the two, and the next Orbit tag closes the gap.
